+{
+  // TRAINING - Docs/IDLE-POWER-OPTIONS.md, option 1. Gold buys power past the level caps.
+  //
+  // INERT WITHOUT CODE. Nothing reads this file until the code plan in Docs/IDLE-POWER-OPTIONS.md
+  // (option 1) is built: ContentDatabase.LoadTraining, PlayerProfile.Training, the last stage of
+  // StatMath.ForHero, GameSession.BuyTrainingRank and the save block.
+  //
+  // NOT PART OF ContentDatabase.ContentVersion, for guild-tech.json's reason: a guild dungeon fight
+  // hands CombatSimulation an empty profile, so it cannot read a rank.
+  //
+  // THE FAMILIES ARE guild-tech.json's FOUR (line, blade, grace, reach), by id, so a role belongs to
+  // the same family in both trees. A rank is worth `share` of the hero's power, compounding, split
+  // equally by power over the family's rungStats (GuildTech.ApplyShare). It applies after guild tech.
+  //
+  // NOTHING HERE IS RANDOM. A rank has one price and one effect, shown before the tap.
+  "currency": "Gold",
+  // Bought Gold (Sealed) is refused, as the Quartermaster refuses it. With Sealed Gold accepted the
+  // reference whale led the non-spender by +40 to +53 percent from 3-6 on (the R24 limit is 6).
+  "refusesSealed": true,
+  // It opens with the chapter 1 finale cleared, where the level caps start to bind: the "training"
+  // row of onboarding.json's unlock table, the only place an opening is decided.
+  // Rank r of a family (from 0) costs firstRankCost * costGrowth^r and adds share, compounding:
+  // a family at rank r carries (1 + share)^r - 1 of its heroes' power.
+  "firstRankCost": 20000,
+  "costGrowth": 1.10,
+  "share": 0.05,
+  "families": ["line", "blade", "grace", "reach"]
+}
